# Which environment variables the deployment pipeline moves, and how far.
#
# ONE definition, read by three things that must never disagree:
#
#   scripts/push-github-secrets.sh   local .env            -> GitHub secrets
#   scripts/sync-vercel-env.mjs      GitHub secrets (CD)   -> Vercel project env
#   .github/workflows/cd.yml         names the secrets it forwards
#
# If these lists drifted, the failure is silent and expensive: a variable the
# app needs is simply absent in production, and Next.js does not complain at
# build time — it fails on the first request that reaches the missing value.
#
# Columns:  NAME  SCOPE  REQUIREMENT
#
#   SCOPE = runtime   the deployed application reads it. Pushed to GitHub AND
#                     synced to the Vercel project (production + preview).
#   SCOPE = deploy    only the CD workflow reads it. Pushed to GitHub and
#                     NEVER written to the Vercel project — the running app has
#                     no business holding a token that can redeploy itself.
#
#   REQUIREMENT = required   absent => the push/sync fails loudly.
#               = optional   absent => skipped with a note.
#
# Deliberately ABSENT from this file, and therefore from GitHub and Vercel:
#
#   DATABASE_PASSWORD, SUPABASE_DB_HOST, SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF
#       Migration-only. CLAUDE.md: "The application itself never opens a
#       Postgres connection — it goes through PostgREST." Shipping a database
#       password to a web host that cannot use it is pure blast radius.
#
#   E2E_TEST_MODE, E2E_RESET_SECRET
#       resolveTestMode() throws under NODE_ENV=production. Never send them.

AUTH_SECRET                              runtime  required
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID                           runtime  required
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET                       runtime  required
AUTH_URL                                 runtime  required
AUTH_TRUST_HOST                          runtime  required

NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY        runtime  required
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_NUMBER  runtime  required

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL                 runtime  required
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY     runtime  required
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY                runtime  required
GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY              runtime  required

# Which sign-in path /login offers: `authjs` (default) or `supabase`.
AUTH_PROVIDER                            runtime  optional
# Server-side debug disclosure. `1` turns it on; anything else leaves it off.
# push-github-secrets.sh refuses to promote `1` — see PRODUCTION_REFUSALS there.
APP_DEBUG_ERRORS                         runtime  optional

VERCEL_TOKEN                             deploy   required
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID                        deploy   required
# Only needed when the token is personal rather than scoped to the team that
# owns the project. A team-scoped token resolves the project without it.
VERCEL_TEAM_ID                           deploy   optional
